---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description={`Important limitations on the security information published by ${SITE.name}, including authorised-testing requirements and no-warranty terms.`}
  lede="Read this before acting on anything published here."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Template notice:</strong> this disclaimer is a
    good-faith starting point, not legal advice. Have it reviewed by a qualified
    practitioner in your jurisdiction.
  </div>

  <h2>Educational purpose</h2>
  <p>
    All content on {SITE.name} is published for <strong>educational and defensive
    security purposes only</strong>. Attack techniques are described so that defenders can
    recognise, detect and prevent them — not so they can be reproduced against systems the
    reader has no right to touch.
  </p>

  <h2>Authorised testing only</h2>
  <p>
    Any security testing technique referenced here must only be performed against systems
    you own, or for which you hold explicit written authorisation. Unauthorised access to
    computer systems is a criminal offence under the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (US), the
    Computer Misuse Act (UK), and equivalent legislation in most jurisdictions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      You are solely responsible for how you apply this information, and for ensuring your
      actions are lawful where you are.
    </strong>
  </p>

  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing here constitutes professional security, legal, compliance or financial advice.
    Security decisions depend on your specific threat model, architecture, regulatory
    obligations and risk tolerance. Engage a qualified practitioner who can assess your
    actual environment.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Content is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. Security is a fast-moving
    field: techniques, tooling behaviour, vendor defaults and threat activity all change.
    An article that was accurate on its publication date may not be accurate today. Always
    verify against current primary sources before acting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Configuration examples and code samples are illustrative. Test them in a non-production
    environment and adapt them to your context before deploying. Applying a configuration
    from an article without understanding it can reduce your security posture rather than
    improve it.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {SITE.organization.legalName} accepts no
    liability for any loss or damage — including data loss, service disruption, financial
    loss or security incidents — arising from use of, or reliance on, anything published
    here.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party products</h2>
  <p>
    Mentions of vendors, products or open-source projects are for identification and
    analysis. They do not constitute endorsement. Trademarks belong to their respective
    owners. Any commercial relationship relevant to a piece of coverage is disclosed within
    that article, per our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    We are not responsible for the content, accuracy or security of external sites we link
    to.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or concerns:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
